#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# pochhammer

#% text
# `pochhammer(a, n)` gives the rising factorial a (a + 1) ... (a + n - 1).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For integer n it is the product; negative n give 1/((a - 1) ... (a + n)).

#% item
# Otherwise gamma(a + n)/gamma(a), evaluated for numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
pochhammer(a, 3)
#% output
#= a*(1 + a)*(2 + a)

#% cell
pochhammer(2, 3)
#% output
#= 24

#% cell
pochhammer(1/2, 2)
#% output
#= 3/4

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
pochhammer(2.5, 1.5)
#% output
#= 4.51351666838205

#% cell
pochhammer(a, -2)
#% output
#= 1/((-2 + a)*(-1 + a))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `factorial_power`, `gamma`, `binomial`
